```html
<style>
  .save { background: #244fc7; transition: background-color 160ms ease; }
  .save:hover, .save:focus-visible { background: #17368f; }
  .saving { animation: pulse 900ms ease-in-out infinite alternate; }
  @keyframes pulse { from { opacity: 0.55; } to { opacity: 1; } }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .saving { animation: none; } }
</style>
<button class="save saving">Saving</button>
```
The state color uses a transition; the repeated status signal uses keyframes and has a reduced-motion alternative.

```html
<style>
  .notice { transform: translateY(0); opacity: 1; transition: transform 180ms ease, opacity 180ms ease; }
  .notice[data-state="entering"] { transform: translateY(-0.75rem); opacity: 0; }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .notice { transition: none; } }
</style>
<p class="notice" data-state="settled">Profile saved.</p>
```
The transform changes the painted position while the paragraph's layout box remains in place.

```html
<style>
  .status { opacity: 1; transform: none; }
  .status.is-complete { animation: arrive 500ms ease-out 1 both; }
  @keyframes arrive {
    0% { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(0.5rem); }
    70% { transform: translateY(-0.1rem); }
    100% { opacity: 1; transform: none; }
  }
</style>
<p class="status is-complete">Upload complete</p>
```
The base status is already visible and complete; keyframes enhance how it arrives.

```html
<style>
  .panel { opacity: 1; transform: none; }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
    .panel { animation: panel-enter 180ms ease-out; }
    @keyframes panel-enter {
      from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(0.75rem); }
      to { opacity: 1; transform: none; }
    }
  }
</style>
<section class="panel" aria-labelledby="panel-title"><h2 id="panel-title">Settings</h2></section>
```
The panel is fully visible by default. Motion is added only when no reduction preference is present.
